title: Payers › Workflow Builder › Start from a template
route: /payers/summit?tab=builder
intro: Five starter workflows, each marked 'Illustrative, not payer policy'. Picking one and naming it makes a draft for this payer; the draft keeps a link to the template it came from, and each rule step is pointed at the payer's own rule when exactly one fits.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Click 'From a template' (New menu)\nor 'Start with a template' (empty state)"
overlay o1 "Right-hand panel 'Start with a template'\n'A new draft for Summit Medicaid HMO. Nothing is used for cases until you publish it.'"
screen l1 "Five choices (radio cards)\nInitial Authorization, Concurrent Review, Reauthorization,\nRetroactive Authorization, Modification\nEach with one description and 'Illustrative, not payer policy.'"
click c1 "Pick one template"
screen f1 "Form appears under the list\n'Name' (placeholder: the template name),\n'Service' (Every service or one level of care),\n'Request type' (set from the template)"
input i1 "Optionally rename it, pick a service and request type"
decision d1 "Is a template picked?"
click c2 "Click 'Create the draft'"
process p1 "Store makes a draft\nState, plan and owner are filled in, start date is the demo date\nEach rule step points at the payer's rule when exactly one fits"
store st1 "Workflow saved as a draft, version 1\nVersion history first line: 'Started from the template'\nEdit log gets an entry"
process p2 "The new draft is selected and opens on the canvas\nThe address becomes ?workflow=the-new-id"
screen s2 "Bar shows the name and a 'Draft' pill\n'Nothing blocks publishing' or the checks that do"
click c3 "Click 'Cancel', X, or press Escape"
process p3 "Panel closes, nothing is created"
end e1 "A draft made from the template is open"
endx e2 "No draft made"

s1 --> o1 --> l1 --> c1 --> f1 --> i1 --> d1
d1 -->|Yes| c2 --> p1 --> st1 --> p2 --> s2 --> e1
d1 -->|No| l1
o1 --> c3 --> p3 --> e2
